    "description": "The Sri Lakshmi Narasimha Swamy Temple or Yadadri or Yadagiri Gutta Devasthanam (YGD), or Pancha Narasimha Kshetram or Rishi Aradhana Kshetram is a Hindu Temple situated on a hillock in the small town of Yadagirigutta in the Yadadri Bhuvanagiri district of the Indian state of Telangana. Yadadri Temple is touted as Telangana's own Tirupati. The Temple is dedicated to the god Narasimha, an Avatar of Vishnu. The temple was expanded and rebuilt between 2016 and March 2022.",
